                        "form": "more unpurposed"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "f3db9f57-8a14-49b3-886d-5742f5c02b58",
                        "entry_id": "82adde3a-4e55-3a48-ab6a-534a047faaa9",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most unpurposed"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "73cdde8a-a5a7-353b-b0f3-17fec2b0f4e8",
                        "entry_id": "82adde3a-4e55-3a48-ab6a-534a047faaa9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Without purpose."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d7ffbbe-45da-4ddb-9577-bd3b425088ea",
                                "sense_id": "73cdde8a-a5a7-353b-b0f3-17fec2b0f4e8",
                                "text": "If that Law did well to reduce from liberty to bondage for an ingratitude not the greatest, much more became it the Law of God to enact the restorement of a free born man from an unpurpos’d, and unworthy bondage to a rightfull liberty for the most unnatural fraud and ingratitude that can be committed against him."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8224a564-efd1-46da-a760-01b471e5cc10",
                                "sense_id": "73cdde8a-a5a7-353b-b0f3-17fec2b0f4e8",
                                "text": "He was distinguished from his fellows by the fact that each year he grew more aware that he hadn’t even a dim candle of talent; that he was ill-planned and unpurposed; that he would have to settle down to the ordinary gray limbo of jobs and offices […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "13cea2af-04ab-4155-88b5-4ff0d32e5c9a",
                                "sense_id": "73cdde8a-a5a7-353b-b0f3-17fec2b0f4e8",
                                "text": "‘Your questions about Mrs Jepp, I can’t possibly answer them, ‘said Mervyn, looking at his watch but unpurposed, settling into his chair […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "aadb689e-764b-31ba-8839-f27132dcce7f",
                        "entry_id": "82adde3a-4e55-3a48-ab6a-534a047faaa9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not deliberate."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8b743222-0eb5-40a7-820e-8f2b92788771",
                                "sense_id": "aadb689e-764b-31ba-8839-f27132dcce7f",
                                "text": "When I did make thee free, sworest thou not then\nTo do this when I bade thee? Do it at once;\nOr thy precedent services are all\nBut accidents unpurposed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0bd77fb5-e3c5-41ab-9f3f-8fa89f25b646",
                                "sense_id": "aadb689e-764b-31ba-8839-f27132dcce7f",
                                "text": "1640, William Whately, Prototypes, London: Edward Langham, The Thirteenth Example, pp. 199-200,\n[…] the Lord will surely accept him and forgive his unpurposed offences and sinnes of meere weakenesse and frailty."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e9c25385-1467-45ac-a88c-2fc3fd1d7437",
                                "sense_id": "aadb689e-764b-31ba-8839-f27132dcce7f",
                                "text": "It was written in very small characters—perhaps an unpurposed indication of the misgivings with which she allowed herself to pen the words."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "47c3083d-f65f-40f0-b8b0-0e43b919f455",
                                "sense_id": "aadb689e-764b-31ba-8839-f27132dcce7f",
                                "text": "O pitying strangers, since ye will not hear\nMy old blind father, for some tales ye have heard\nOf his unpurposed sin, Oh, still give ear\nTo a lost maiden, and accept the word\nI speak for his sake […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
